  "_meta": {
    "what": "Empirical EVM DIV/MOD/SDIV/SMOD operand distribution for Phase 3 of the DIV-perf effort. See docs/divmod-evm-workload.md.",
    "source": "real mainnet transactions, opcode-level debug_traceTransaction (drpc.org), frequency-weighted over the sample (every executed division counts once)",
    "sample": "32 distinct blocks, 25238313..25431308 (~27 days, June 2026), 145888 division ops (138601 unsigned DIV+MOD core). UNION of two collection runs (count=25 stride=7919 head-3001; plus count=30 stride=9973 from head, of which only 4 blocks completed before the endpoint throttled) plus a 3-block probe -- so block spacing is mostly 7919 with an irregular tail; three block pairs are 6 apart. NOT reproducible from a single command; the exact 32-block list is in block_list below.",
    "block_list": [25238313,25246232,25254151,25262070,25269989,25277908,25285827,25293746,25301665,25309584,25317503,25325422,25333341,25341260,25349179,25357098,25365017,25372936,25380855,25388774,25396693,25401389,25404612,25411356,25411362,25412531,25420450,25421329,25421335,25428369,25431302,25431308],
    "reproduce": "zcat bench/div-operands-mainnet.jsonl.gz | python3 scripts/analyze-div-operands.py /dev/stdin --weights bench/div-weights.json  (regenerates this file byte-for-byte except this _meta block)",
    "n_definition": "divisor word-count: 0 (b==0), 1 (<2^64), 2 (<2^128), 3 (<2^192), 4 (<2^256)",
    "HOW_TO_WEIGHT": "Use the 'partition' block: a NON-OVERLAPPING partition of ALL divides that sums to 1.0 (precedence a<b > pow2 > genuine-by-n). Do NOT add a_lt_b_frac+pow2_frac -- they overlap ~15pp (byte-extraction with zero high bytes is both). cheap_frac = a_lt_b_frac + pow2(not a<b) + b0.",
    "pow2_caveat": "pow2_byte_aligned_frac of the 0.46 pow2 class are divisor==2^(8k) byte/word-extraction idioms (dominated by 2^224 and 2^160), NOT Q96/Q128 fixed-point (which is only ~3% of pow2). These are real executed DIV opcodes so a shift path helps them, but the mix is contract-vintage-sensitive (modern Solidity emits SHR).",
    "stability": "Per-block cheap% ranges 30%..93% (stdev 19pp); block-bootstrap 95% CI on the 54% op-weighted cheap figure is [48.4%, 60.5%]. Biggest single block = 12.4% of ops, top 10 of 32 = 51%. Headline survives dropping the dominant block (54.1->54.6%).",
    "known_bias": "The heaviest ~3-8% of txs (largest aggregator/MEV swaps) drop to server-side trace timeouts (148 logged failures across the runs) and are NOT sampled. Their op-density and divisor mix are unmeasured, so the bias DIRECTION is unproven -- do not assume it is conservative."
  },
